><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>ROBERT A. MAMMANO: 'Charging the new batteries-IC controller track new technologies' IEEE AESS SYSTEMS MAGAZINE 1995, pages 20 - 25, XP002930755</text><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1107344A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAIZONO YOSHINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAIZONO, YOSHINORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAIZONO YOSHINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAIZONO, YOSHINORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The invention provides a protective circuit for protecting a secondary battery from damage due to continuous use with excessive current and a protective device for use in the protective circuit. A main protective circuit (A) includes main control means (1) for turning off a first FET (11) or a second FET (12) in response to excessive charging, excessive discharging or excessive discharge current of a secondary battery (3). An auxiliary protective circuit (B) includes auxiliary control means (2) for turning off a third FET (13) if the main control means (1) does not properly function. The secondary battery (3) is thus protected by the duplicate protection.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un circuit de protection évitant à un accumulateur secondaire d'être endommagé par l'utilisation continue d'un courant excessif, et sur un dispositif de protection destiné à être utilisé dans ce circuit. Un circuit (A) de protection principal comprend un organe de commande (1) principal réagissant à la charge et à la décharge excessives de courant d'un accumulateur secondaire (3). Un circuit (B) de protection auxiliaire comprend un organe de commande (2) auxiliaire destiné à bloquer un transistor à effet de champs (13) si l'organe de commande (1) principal ne fonctionne pas correctement. L'accumulateur secondaire (3) a ainsi une double protection.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>